4. nist-sha2-selected.json
--------------------------

Selected from the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST), Cryptographic Algorithm
Validation Program (CAVP), SHA byte-oriented test vectors. Credit belongs to NIST/CAVP.

Source: https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-algorithm-validation-program/secure-hashing
Archive: https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/shs/shabytetestvectors.zip
Source revision: CAVS 11.0, SHA-256 and SHA-512 ShortMsg files generated on 2011-03-15,
pinned by the archive and source-file hashes below; selection verified on 2026-10-29.

  shabytetestvectors.zip
      SHA-256 929ef80b7b3418aca026643f6f248815913b60e01741a44bba9e118067f4c9b8
  shabytetestvectors/SHA256ShortMsg.rsp (inside the archive)
      SHA-256 75e1cb83994638481808e225b9eb0c1ebd0c232d952ac42b61abce6363be283c
  shabytetestvectors/SHA512ShortMsg.rsp (inside the archive)
      SHA-256 e53a36c03609e5a3e3cc4b6e117a499db7864c23ec825c6cec99503a45f40764
  nist-sha2-selected.json (the file in this directory)
      SHA-256 bc19af461d0ca94d5f4b94228da209fbb3b6e1112cc123fde047deff7063371e

Changed by ZeroJ on 2026-10-29: selected 21 byte-aligned message/digest pairs (8 SHA-256 and
13 SHA-512), including empty messages and padding boundaries, and converted the response-file
format to JSON. The JSON records the algorithm, source filename, length in bytes, message and
digest, with source URL/hash metadata. NIST's Len = 0, Msg = 00 notation is represented by an
empty message string; other message bytes and all expected digest bytes are unchanged.
The archive and response files are not vendored in this directory. The existing
assurance/sha2-circom/verify-nist-source.py checks the archive pin and every selected pair.

